course: dictionary
lesson: 12059
title: Asking for clarification
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A clarification is an explanation that makes something clearer. It comes from the word clear, so when you ask for clarification, you are asking for something to be made easier to understand.
explain: In class, you can say «Could I ask for clarification, please?» when the instructions are confusing. It is a polite way of saying, «Could you explain that again?»
explain: Officials and newspapers also give a clarification after a statement that people found confusing. The clarification tells the reader what was meant. In cooking and science, clarification means something different: making a liquid clear by removing bits from it.
fact: A clarification is an explanation that makes something clearer or easier to understand.
fact: «Clarification» is a noun, and it is usually uncountable: you can say «some clarification» but not «a clarifications».
fact: Useful phrases include «ask for clarification», «seek clarification» and «for clarification».
fact: In science and cooking, clarification means making a liquid clear by removing bits from it, such as clarifying butter.
fact: When you ask for clarification in class, you are being polite and sensible, not silly.
exercise: «Mrs Patel gave us a clarification of the homework rules.» What does clarification mean here? | A loud shout across the classroom | A long list of new words | A mistake in the homework | *An explanation that makes the rules clearer
exercise: «I did not understand question three, so I asked for clarification.» What did I ask for? | A surprise test | A new pencil | *An explanation, so that the question was easier to understand | A longer break
exercise: In cooking, clarification of butter means | Mixing the butter with milk | Adding sugar and spices to the butter | *Removing the bits so the butter becomes clear | Cooling the butter in the fridge overnight
test: «The news office issued a clarification after its confusing report.» What was the clarification for? | *To make the confusing report clearer | To cancel the news for ever | To tell a joke about the news | To make the report longer
test: Which sentence uses clarification correctly? | «I clarification my lunch to the teacher.» | «The clarification ran very fast across the field.» | «Could you give me a clarifications of the rule, please?» | *«Could you give me some clarification of the rule, please?»
exam: «When the instructions were unclear, Sam asked the teacher for clarification, and the teacher explained the task again.» What does asking for clarification mean? | Refusing to do the task at all | Shouting the answer out to the class | Writing a new story instead | *Politely asking someone to explain something again
